# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

This repository is a fork of the original "mod-audio" project. The fork modernizes the architecture, migrates services toward FastAPI, and opens the platform to custom hardware integrations. The new project name and branding are introduced in this changelog and the top-level README.

## 1.0.0 - 2025-10-01 — Initial fork release (MADELINE)

  - chore: repository forked from `mod-audio` and reorganized for modular services
  - feat: reworked API surface and migration path toward FastAPI for web services
  - feat: decoupled audio processing service to enable running on dedicated hardware
  - feat: added `modhost` bridge and session manager refactors for better hardware integration
  - chore: removed ad-hoc analysis scripts from project root and archived them under `cleanup-archive/`
  - docs: updated README and CHANGELOG to describe fork and migration plan
  - ci: added minimal test harness and development tasks (see README)

Notes:
  - The project is now named "MADELINE" (Madeline). The short nickname `mado` (Madeline Audio Device Orchestrator) is also suggested for CLI/package usage.

---

## Legacy history

The full historical changelog from upstream `mod-audio` has been preserved (see legacy/ or original repository tags). The entries that predate this fork are considered legacy and are available for reference in the project history. Future entries will follow semantic versioning starting from 1.0.0.
